# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository on all platforms,
# regardless of a clone's local `core.autocrlf`. Without this, a Windows
# checkout can commit CRLF blobs that every other platform then reads back
# differently, and byte-exact comparisons start failing on one platform only.
#
# This is the git-layer half of the discipline. The runtime half ships with
# the cross-platform skill: `skills/gzs-cross-platform-python/scripts/
# audit_portability.py --check line-endings` fails closed on any committed
# text surface still carrying CRLF, and on the absence of this directive.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git must never line-ending-normalize. `text=auto` already
# detects most of these, but naming them keeps detection out of the loop for
# the formats this repository actually ships.
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
